I think I should call the attention of the house to the ruling which His Honour the Speaker gave in connection with airing grievances such as have been aired tonight. He pointed out that it was perfectly in order for an hon. member to raise any grievance;
but, having done so, if some other member raised another grievance, it was not permissible to go back to the grievance first raised.
I did not want to interrupt the hon. member when he was speaking, but I think I should call the attention of hon. members to that ruling, by which we must be governed.
